        "original_id": "f236b061-ac55-5b5f-b8f3-2e34fd001a67",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kang Sung-yeon, Jang Hyuk, Han Ye-seul, Kim Min-joon, Son Hyun-joo, Kim Kap-soo, Prince Yeonsan, Jang Nok-su\n- Works: King and the Clown, Tazza\n- Companies: Cinema Service, CJ Entertainment\n- Topics: South Korean film, South Korean television\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, Kang Sung-yeon rose to fame by playing Prince Yeonsan's concubine Jang Nok-su in the period film King and the Clown.\n- In 2005, King and the Clown drew 12.3 admissions and at that time became the highest-grossing domestic film in Korean cinema history.\n- King and the Clown was released on 29 December 2005, has a runtime of 119 minutes, and was distributed domestically by Cinema Service and internationally by CJ Entertainment.\n- Tazza is a 2008 South Korean television series starring Jang Hyuk, Han Ye-seul, Kim Min-joon, Kang Sung-yeon, Son Hyun-joo, and Kim Kap-soo.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4cd68720-faf3-52d4-9355-162cc0f734b2",
        "text": "Page: Kang Sung-yeon. Sentence: Then in 2005, Kang rose to fame when she played Prince Yeonsan's concubine Jang Nok-su in \"King and the Clown\", a period film that drew 12.3 admissions, making it (at the time) the highest-grossing domestic film in Korean cinema history.\nPage: King and the Clown. Sentence: It was released on 29 December 2005, runs for 119 minutes; and distributed domestically by Cinema Service and internationally by CJ Entertainment.\nPage: Tazza (TV series). Sentence: Tazza () is a 2008 South Korean television series starring Jang Hyuk, Han Ye-seul, Kim Min-joon, Kang Sung-yeon, Son Hyun-joo and Kim Kap-soo.",
